cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "bounded-lognorm: bounded lognormal distributions for scipy.stats"
abstract: >-
  Two bounded lognormal distributions, each mode/sigma-parametrized on a
  finite interval and implemented as a full scipy.stats.rv_continuous
  subclass: BL2, a smooth geometric-mean form with a speed/precision dial,
  and BL, the original piecewise form, entirely in closed form.
authors:
  - family-names: Teske
    given-names: Ted
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-11-04"
license: MIT
# Concept DOI: all versions, always resolving to the latest. Each release's
# own DOI is listed on that Zenodo record (0.2.1: 10.5281/zenodo.23898464;
# 0.2.0: 10.5281/zenodo.23897349).
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23897348
repository-code: "https://github.com/tedteske/bounded_lognorm"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/bounded-lognorm/"
keywords:
  - statistics
  - probability distribution
  - bounded lognormal
  - lognormal
  - scipy
  - Monte Carlo
